bergdb-workload 1
# A decrease of the startup distance after the stream has grown past twice the new
# setting (bergdb 012-09, part 1, finding F1): 400 values of 30000 bytes with a startup
# distance of 5000000, then setsd 400000 and 150 more. While D's span is longer than
# twice the new setting, the take's deadline is the span (TransSeq.take, span();
# 007-03, D4; 007-07), and takes stop at transactions that twice the setting alone
# would take, as in MakeStreams' stream deadline. No restarts, no reclaim, so that
# C's bergdb-run runs it whole (012-09 proper, section 6.6). cross.sh runs it in the
# full set only (workloads/full/); sdcut.wl is its smaller copy in both sets.

